# cpp slice: the committed crossing counts, nounk build (the campaign gate and wp5_gate/nounk_gate compare every '  P'/'  U' row).
# Re-taken 2026-09-28 for the optimisation unit's step 8d (X-2, the pull family): NEW rows only, 'decode pull' (walked in
#   place), 'decode pull drained' (ak_bdr_footprint + ak_bdr_drain in AK_BDR_MIN_CHUNK chunks) and, full build, 'decode
#   pull retain', per payload: reverse 0 and records = push's reverse count (ABI v1 7.1's invariant, checked on each row);
#   every existing row is identical to the previous file (diffed before replacing it).
# Re-taken 2026-09-27 for FIX-PLAN WP8 (CAMPAIGN req 19 as amended; ABI v1 decision 11 rules 7 and 8):
#   - a retain decode makes ONE ak_dec_reset_<Root> (before it; the options stay at a stable per-thread address and the
#     context stays armed), not two: every 'decode retain' row is 1 forward lower (107 rows, full build);
#   - unk_grow grows geometrically (at least double the old capacity, at least 64 B, clamped to INT32_MAX), in the
#     counting build as in the timed one: 18 U-* 'decode retain' rows make fewer reverse (grow) calls, e.g. U-leaf-all
#     18 -> 8, U-deep-all 16 -> 10; no other row changes. The no-unknown build has no retain row and is unchanged.
# Earlier (2026-09-26, WP7, R-H31): forward includes every exported entry point the timed loop calls -- host =
# ak_enc_reset inside each encode_into_* and the retain decode's reset, take = the loop's ak_enc_take; retain rows
# (no pre-placed buffer) and the 92 U-* rows at the shapes roots.
# counts binary built from the working tree at a4533fc9d + the WP8 changes; deterministic.
counting build, linkage=shared, -std=201703
Per-element columns are forward / reverse. forward = core + host + take (req 19):
host = ak_enc_reset inside each encode_into_* (before the encode entry point) and the
one ak_dec_reset_<Root> of a retain decode (before it; rule 7); take = the timed loop's
ak_enc_take after an encode. Retain: no pre-placed buffer, geometric grow (rule 8).

